# Build context for `az acr build` and any repo-root `docker build`.
# Every VRSky Dockerfile uses the repo ROOT as its build context. This
# allowlists only the sources the images actually COPY, keeping the ~1.8 GB
# working copy out of the upload: .git, data/, node_modules, ui/node_modules,
# and the stray compiled binaries sitting at src/ root (git-ignored but on disk).
#
# Docker negation rule: to re-include a path you must first re-include its
# parent dir, THEN exclude the unwanted children — hence the !dir / dir/* / !dir/keep triples.
*

# --- Go services: source only, NOT the stray compiled binaries at src/ root ---
!src
src/*
!src/go.mod
!src/go.sum
!src/cmd
!src/pkg
!src/internal

# --- UI: all source except installed deps / build output ---
# The rest used to sit in ui/.dockerignore, which a repo-root build never
# reads. ui/Dockerfile copies none of it: local test output, env files
# (which may hold secrets), logs and editor droppings.
!ui
ui/node_modules
ui/dist
ui/coverage
ui/.nyc_output
ui/**/*.lcov
ui/.env*
ui/**/*.log
ui/**/*-debug.log*
ui/**/yarn-error.log*
ui/.eslintcache
ui/**/.DS_Store

# --- DB migrations are bundled into the management-api image ---
!infrastructure
infrastructure/*
!infrastructure/migrations
